#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261590 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b492068c-2bd2-5611-baab-780959d24c3d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of an Inverse Function Using a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bcbf1ad-7d2c-5e0f-b862-1b9f5468ca70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bcbf1ad-7d2c-5e0f-b862-1b9f5468ca70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261592} :answer-field/id #uuid "14979071-2702-5196-aef9-77c4e25a2ed5" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2fbff772-e6e5-5110-9b66-ccc497ff0d44" :question/math-academy-id "q-75829" :question/problem "The following table gives the values of functions $f(x)$ and ${f}^{'}(x)$ at some points. Find $({f}^{-1})^{'}(3).$\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{'}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $-9$ | $0$ |\n| $5$ | $3$ | $-2$ |\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{'}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{'}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{'}(3)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{'}({f}^{-1}(3))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(3)=5$ and ${f}^{'}(5)=-2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{'}(3) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{'}({f}^{-1}(3))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{'}(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
